<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Paladin Healer in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar, Naxxramas, Obsidian Sanctum, and Eye of Eternity. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 2</h2>
<i>Healer gearing always heavily depends on playstyle, situation and raid environment so treat the BiS list below as a guideline rather than a gospel.</i>
<br/>
<br/>Due to being able to wear all 4 armor types, Holy Paladin gearing can be somewhat overwhelming as it has a ton of options. With a little bit of work and stat evaluations, we can cut this down tremendously and also consider loot priority carefully, as mail and plate spellpower gear is very uncontested in return.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="when-to-switch-from-4pc-t7">When to Switch From 4pc T7 to 4pc T8</h3>The power of the 4pc T7 set means that for Holy Paladins in Phase 2, it requires several simultaneous tier slot upgrades to replace it. The general rule of thumb is, you will need one of the following conditions to be true to drop 4pc T7:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Two 25m non-tier upgrades</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Two 25m T8 slots (not the chest)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Three 10m T8 slots (not the chest)</div></li></ul>When any of these conditions are true, you can drop 4pc T7 entirely and you should then be free to transition entirely into getting individual upgrades, until you achieve the 4pc T8 set. As pointed out, the tier chest is ALMOST ALWAYS the offpiece in T8, due to how poorly itemized it is and how many possible upgrades there are for it. The only time this should not be the case is if you've had zero chest drops from your T7 chest.<br/>
<br/>Due to the overall strength of 4pc T8, it's not realistic to drop the 4pc set bonus despite the tier only being ilvl 232 (as opposed to 252 HM pieces). You must ALWAYS use the chest as an offpiece, there are a lot of options for chest offpieces and the tier option in this slot is horrible.<br/>As soon as you have 4pc T8 available, whether it's through any mix of 10m and 25m tier, you should equip it, as long as it's not the chest. Because the ilvl difference between 10m and 25m tier for T8 is only 7 ilvls, being forced to use 10m tier is a very marginal difference compared to in T7 10m vs 25m tier.<br/>
<br/>As a final note, if you have more than one Holy Paladin in your roster, you may be tempted to look at sets that do not use the T8 4pc. The shoulders and gloves slots do have higher EP non-tier items; however, there are several 2-tank fights in the tier, meaning the second Sacred Shield still has use. Additionally, the actual total EP difference between wearing tier and not in these two slots is very minimal. For this reason, we recommend still aiming for the 4pc, then using your own judgement to drop these items in 1-tank fights only.<br/>
<br/>
