<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Conquest for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 2</h3>Only a couple of the items that are purchaseable via <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=221/emblem-of-conquest">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_championsgrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Conquest</span></span></a> are good for Holy Paladin; unfortunately, the buyable tier tokens are helm and chest, so only one tier item is good for us. The belt is okay, but is eclipsed by the craftable belt. The off-set legs and gloves are okay, but those are 2 tier slots and it's generally going to be better to equip even the 10m tier over those items. Lastly, the neck is not worth purchasing in any scenario, so it is omitted.<br/>
<br/>Prioritize purchasing the helm. By the time you've gotten it, you can look to see if you have any weak slots that can be temporarily covered with other purchases, but all other items are mediocre at best and it wouldn't be a big deal to just ignore these purchases altogether.<br/>
