<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 2</h3>The trinket situation is largely the same as in Phase 1 for Holy Paladin; however, once you get <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46051/meteorite-crystal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_dungeon_ulduarraid_misc_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Meteorite Crystal</span></a>, you're basically set for trinkets for the rest of the expansion.<br/>
<br/>The new major player is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46051/meteorite-crystal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_dungeon_ulduarraid_misc_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Meteorite Crystal</span></a>, which becomes BiS in all situations. Always equip and make sure to use the on:use as often as possible. The only rules to observe for the duration are to NOT STOP CASTING, as well as ONLY to cast your healing spells. Due to how <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53563/beacon-of-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_beaconoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beacon of Light</span></a> works, you get 2 stacks per cast with any heal that goes through Beacon, making Holy Paladin the fastest stacker of this trinket and therefore making it worth roughly 160-170 MP5 on the lower end. Playing around this trinket primarily means to avoid using Judgement, recasting Beacon, or Sacred Shield during its on:use. That being said, it's not the end of the world if you do, but this is a minor aspect to min/<wbr/>max when playing the class.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=37111/soul-preserver">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_orb_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Preserver</span></a> continues to be very powerful as a second option. As before, it's worth about 50 MP5 per target you heal (at 30 casts per minute - it goes up with more). Each heal of <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41106/glyph-of-holy-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glyph_majorpaladin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Holy Light</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53563/beacon-of-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_beaconoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beacon of Light</span></a> count as an extra target, so with high CPM and a stacked raid, you can still have this trinket pumping out over 400 MP5. This ensures its place as a trinket contender for Holy Paladin through the whole expansion.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44255/darkmoon-card-greatness">
